and for the decisions that are being made. And I want

01:32:09.975 --> 01:32:13.767
you to know that every decision that I have been involved in, I think deeply

01:32:14.267 --> 01:32:17.485
about this community and the long-term benefits and impacts of those decisions

01:32:17.517 --> 01:32:20.867
that we make. I've been here a

01:32:21.367 --> 01:32:24.185
little while now. This is my 5th year on council, and prior to that I

01:32:24.233 --> 01:32:26.862
served 4 years on the Planning Commission. I've learned a few things.

01:32:28.096 --> 01:32:31.542
We've gotten some things right and made some mistakes.

01:32:32.343 --> 01:32:34.475
Hopefully we've learned— hopefully I've learned from those.

01:32:35.469 --> 01:32:39.204
But I'm really grateful for the opportunity to serve. I always

01:32:39.300 --> 01:32:42.105
think my mother lives here. I was the first person in my family to move

01:32:42.605 --> 01:32:46.295
to Eagle Mountain. As a consequence of that, my sister

01:32:46.795 --> 01:32:49.586
and brother-in-law moved here. My mother now lives here and has for a number of

01:32:50.086 --> 01:32:54.339
years. My daughter bought a home and is making Eagle

01:32:54.839 --> 01:32:57.855
Mountain her home with 3 of my grandchildren. My son lives in a home here

01:32:58.355 --> 01:33:00.778
in Eagle Mountain and has 3 of my other grandchildren who are here.

01:33:01.548 --> 01:33:04.262
I wish my son who lives in California would get a clue and come and

01:33:04.762 --> 01:33:07.570
join us and enjoy it, but he lives in Santa Barbara.

01:33:08.455 --> 01:33:10.763
It's the coastline that drew him away, I'm afraid.

01:33:11.667 --> 01:33:14.991
I'm just really grateful to the people of Eagle Mountain and to those that live

01:33:15.491 --> 01:33:17.558
in this valley. And I'm grateful to those who sit here with me,

01:33:19.252 --> 01:33:23.027
who we arm wrestle. Anybody that thinks that we come

01:33:23.140 --> 01:33:25.996
to a decision or to an answer easily and that we're all on the same

01:33:26.044 --> 01:33:29.434
page, I'd love for you to just sit on my shoulder during some of the

01:33:29.934 --> 01:33:32.033
phone conversations that I've had with each of these individuals.

01:33:32.130 --> 01:33:35.553
Thank you. It's pretty rowdy.

01:33:35.906 --> 01:33:40.041
That's probably the best way I can describe it. We disagree quite often,

01:33:41.196 --> 01:33:44.642
but we temper one another and we try to educate one another. I'm really grateful

01:33:45.142 --> 01:33:49.130
for their input. Lastly, I just want to say I'm really grateful for our

01:33:49.194 --> 01:33:52.641
people that work here. I own a small

01:33:53.141 --> 01:33:57.177
business in Lehi, and I've said this often and I mean it. The backbone

01:33:57.209 --> 01:34:00.704
of my business is my people. My employees are,

01:34:01.459 --> 01:34:04.751
are, are, they are the glue and the

01:34:05.251 --> 01:34:09.006
mechanism that makes my company successful. And I truly believe

01:34:09.022 --> 01:34:12.426
that Eagle Mountain City, that each of those that you see

01:34:12.490 --> 01:34:16.279
seated here and around the periphery of this room, each of them

01:34:16.568 --> 01:34:20.518
are what hold this city together and make a difference in your daily lives,

01:34:20.566 --> 01:34:23.071
whether you recognize it or not. So thank you to each of them.

01:34:27.411 --> 01:34:31.199
So I just wanted to add a little bit of additional information

01:34:31.231 --> 01:34:35.230
to the youth city council activity at

01:34:35.730 --> 01:34:38.388
my home this Thursday night. So it's for any youth in the city,

01:34:39.210 --> 01:34:43.220
and it will involve horseback riding and

01:34:43.253 --> 01:34:46.939
dancing, a costume contest, pumpkin carving contest.

01:34:47.052 --> 01:34:50.142
It's a free event. If you want to participate in

01:34:50.158 --> 01:34:53.149
the pumpkin carving contest, Bring your own pre-carved pumpkin,

01:34:54.075 --> 01:34:57.651
and we're gonna have a lot of fun. Mayor's gonna be there with me.

01:34:58.580 --> 01:35:02.063
Other city council members, if you wanna come join in, you're welcome to come

01:35:02.079 --> 01:35:05.627
to the house. But anyway, we're just— we're gonna

01:35:06.127 --> 01:35:09.509
have a lot of fun time with the youth, and encourage

01:35:09.750 --> 01:35:13.302
any youth you know to come. It's at 2441 East Cedar

01:35:13.802 --> 01:35:16.368
Drive this Thursday night. Thank you.

01:35:20.072 --> 01:35:23.894
I'm pleased to see people here. I hope you're here for some of

01:35:23.926 --> 01:35:27.057
the items that— I suspect I know what some of you are

01:35:27.557 --> 01:35:31.119
here for. And I'm grateful that you're engaging in the process.

01:35:31.938 --> 01:35:35.615
I've said this many times, I think that we are much better when

01:35:35.727 --> 01:35:39.998
we have more active people in the community to help us to see where

01:35:40.498 --> 01:35:43.643
some of our problem spots are. There's only 6 of us.

01:35:43.851 --> 01:35:48.008
I mean, we can't be everywhere and we can't see everything, and we, we rely

01:35:48.072 --> 01:35:51.138
heavily on our residents to let us know where some of our problem

01:35:51.638 --> 01:35:53.754
areas are. So when you come in and tell us, I can tell you that

01:35:53.770 --> 01:35:57.413
speaking for myself, I listen, and they, they've heard me

01:35:57.913 --> 01:36:00.784
say multiple times, how are we going to address that problem? Um,

01:36:01.747 --> 01:36:06.273
some of the comments that were even made on the, the public, uh, comments section,

01:36:06.850 --> 01:36:09.916
one of them about a sidewalk that we're currently widening right now.

01:36:10.816 --> 01:36:14.059
So I just— I want you to know that it's not falling on deaf ears,

01:36:14.236 --> 01:36:17.543
that we're looking for ways to pay for the

01:36:17.720 --> 01:36:22.360
things that need to be taken care of. And we have to prioritize most

01:36:22.860 --> 01:36:26.551
needful first, obviously. There's a lot of things that are needful,

01:36:26.936 --> 01:36:30.356
and we recognize that. And a lot of times for the residents, it's the one

01:36:30.453 --> 01:36:32.893
that you're facing within 300 feet of your house, usually.

01:36:33.825 --> 01:36:37.092
And And that's not lost on us either. So thank you for being here.

01:36:37.157 --> 01:36:40.767
Thank you for engaging in the process. I hope your experience here is one

01:36:40.783 --> 01:36:44.230
that is positive. My number is

01:36:44.730 --> 01:36:47.272
on our website. If you have any questions, I ask that you call me and

01:36:47.288 --> 01:36:50.281
engage with me. Work's been kind of nuts lately.

01:36:51.060 --> 01:36:53.809
Gentleman up here tried to get a hold of me, and it's been kind of

01:36:53.825 --> 01:36:57.318
nuts the last month. But generally, I try to call back and have

01:36:57.818 --> 01:37:01.458
a conversation with anybody who reaches out to me because I think

01:37:01.958 --> 01:37:02.991
I think it's better to talk than it is to try to engage over social

01:37:03.491 --> 01:37:06.435
media or by text. So that's there available to you. Thanks.

01:37:08.893 --> 01:37:12.301
I also want to welcome everyone that's out here tonight. These meetings are

01:37:12.801 --> 01:37:16.245
no fun when it's just empty seats. It's good to have people

01:37:16.277 --> 01:37:20.244
here that are engaged in their local city government. I've sat

01:37:20.744 --> 01:37:24.546
in those chairs before and addressed the City Council before with, with questions

01:37:25.046 --> 01:37:28.738
and concerns and issues that I've had. These are really exciting times. There's a

01:37:29.238 --> 01:37:33.876
lot going on in our city. We have a major facelift

01:37:34.376 --> 01:37:37.891
with our sewer that's happening. That's a couple hundred million

01:37:38.391 --> 01:37:41.423
dollars that, that we'll be building out.

01:37:42.226 --> 01:37:45.951
We have had some big changes to our property taxes, how those are

01:37:46.451 --> 01:37:49.756
applied. Now every dollar of your property tax goes

01:37:49.772 --> 01:37:53.594
100% to safety is not commingled for any other projects.

01:37:53.642 --> 01:37:57.672
And I think there's a lot of residents that don't know about that change,

01:37:58.523 --> 01:38:01.799
and I think that's important to highlight. We have

01:38:01.895 --> 01:38:05.685
2 wells being built. Those are major, major projects.

01:38:06.263 --> 01:38:09.779
To dig a well on Eagle Mountain, you have to go to about a 1,400-foot

01:38:10.279 --> 01:38:13.392
depth at about 26 inches. So that's a big

01:38:13.892 --> 01:38:17.659
hole in the ground, and those are not cheap to build, but the Major infrastructure

01:38:18.159 --> 01:38:21.665
happening. Pony Express, as you pulled in here, you probably saw the medians being pulled

01:38:22.165 --> 01:38:25.414
out to widen that road. The high-T intersections at

01:38:25.914 --> 01:38:29.098
SR 73 and Ranches Parkway. There's just a lot happening

01:38:29.131 --> 01:38:34.506
within our city. And as Councilmember Wood

01:38:35.006 --> 01:38:38.289
mentioned, there's a lot going on. There's a lot happening and a lot going through

01:38:38.789 --> 01:38:42.117
the dais. And I really try to prepare as much as I can. I spend

01:38:42.133 --> 01:38:45.813
probably 4 to 6 hours before every council meeting reviewing the agenda,

01:38:46.215 --> 01:38:49.300
reviewing each document, each development agreement that comes through here,

01:38:49.927 --> 01:38:53.028
and try to just give it my best effort as

01:38:53.076 --> 01:38:56.531
a representative for the residents of Eagle Mountain. I live here.

01:38:56.756 --> 01:38:59.664
My daughter is soon to be married and will be living here as well.

01:38:59.745 --> 01:39:03.344
My nephew just bought a property in City

01:39:03.844 --> 01:39:06.944
Center, and I'm trying to recruit all my family as well to move out here.

01:39:07.024 --> 01:39:10.711
It's a beautiful place to live. While we're doing this,

01:39:10.871 --> 01:39:13.932
the things that are top of mind— my mind is how do we keep our

01:39:14.432 --> 01:39:17.713
open space? How do we just avoid developing every inch?

01:39:17.858 --> 01:39:20.967
As you drive through Utah County and see that

01:39:21.467 --> 01:39:24.764
development happening, it's hard. It's difficult for cities to do that.

01:39:24.829 --> 01:39:27.761
And I feel like that's a priority for me, to make sure that we retain

01:39:28.498 --> 01:39:31.879
the character of Eagle Mountain as much as we

01:39:31.944 --> 01:39:35.370
possibly can. So I'm excited to have everyone here

01:39:36.451 --> 01:39:38.725
and look forward to our conversation tonight.

01:39:40.710 --> 01:39:44.552
All right, thank you. I just add to everyone else's great comments,

01:39:44.681 --> 01:39:48.071
and I appreciate everyone being here. I have a special

01:39:48.571 --> 01:39:51.709
appreciation today for all the residents and, and staff.

01:39:52.437 --> 01:39:55.949
It takes good people doing good things to make this a

01:39:56.013 --> 01:39:59.724
great place to live, and I think that's what That I mean,

01:39:59.740 --> 01:40:03.676
to see Craig, he's the liaison for the— it's Councilmember Whiting,

01:40:03.692 --> 01:40:06.822
I'm sorry— for the Youth Council. And what does he do? Invites him right into

01:40:07.322 --> 01:40:12.042
his home. And I see our staff doing some amazing things that are

01:40:12.235 --> 01:40:15.552
Herculean efforts of projects that we have right

01:40:16.052 --> 01:40:19.580
now that not very many people would take on. And our staff says, we can

01:40:20.080 --> 01:40:23.985
do that in-house. And it's pretty amazing. So we

01:40:24.485 --> 01:40:27.969
appreciate everybody that has things that contributes to our quality

01:40:28.469 --> 01:40:31.297
of life. Thank you. Eagle Mountain. I just— all of it across the board,

01:40:31.313 --> 01:40:34.503
including our contract personnel with the

01:40:35.003 --> 01:40:38.206
sheriffs and UFA and everybody else. Just a great place to live. So thank you

01:40:38.591 --> 01:40:42.214
for all that you do. With that, we can get started

01:40:42.278 --> 01:40:45.100
with our consent agenda. I know there's a couple items that have to come off

01:40:45.228 --> 01:40:48.098
that we're going to just vote on separately, so there'll be 2 votes, 2 motions.

01:40:49.332 --> 01:40:53.067
Mayor, I'll make the motion, but I have a question, Marcus, about how to do

01:40:53.083 --> 01:40:56.792
this with the 3 items that I need to recuse myself from, do we

01:40:57.292 --> 01:41:00.375
just set those aside and leave them on the consent agenda just separately?

01:41:01.693 --> 01:41:04.987
Yeah, so it depends on how you make the motion. That's what I'm asking specifically.

01:41:05.035 --> 01:41:08.682
So somebody would make the motion to approve the consent

01:41:09.182 --> 01:41:12.378
agenda removing those 3 to be voted on separately. Perfect. That's what we have.

01:41:12.458 --> 01:41:16.764
Then I will make that motion, Mayor. I move that we approve

01:41:16.796 --> 01:41:19.913
the consent agenda removing item 10B,

01:41:20.090 --> 01:41:23.447
10C, and 10D to be voted on separately because I

01:41:23.947 --> 01:41:27.157
want to declare that I, I may have a potential conflict of interest where I

01:41:27.237 --> 01:41:29.582
own a rental home in Firefly.

01:41:30.931 --> 01:41:34.785
Second. Okay, we have a motion by Councilmember Wright and a second by Councilmember

01:41:35.285 --> 01:41:39.170
Clark, and we'll start the vote with Councilmember Wright. Yes. Councilmember Whiting.

01:41:39.347 --> 01:41:43.137
Yes. Councilmember Wood. Yes. Councilmember Hewish. Yes. Councilmember Clark.

01:41:43.297 --> 01:41:46.911
Yes. Okay, we have 3 items left on the consent agenda.

01:41:47.392 --> 01:41:50.869
Mayor, I move that the council approve items 10B,

01:41:51.078 --> 01:41:54.940
10C, and 10D of the consent agenda.

01:41:56.270 --> 01:41:59.395
Second. Okay, we have a motion by Council Member Clark and a second by

01:41:59.895 --> 01:42:02.712
Council Member Whiting, with Council Member Wright, uh,

01:42:03.641 --> 01:42:06.911
abstaining from this vote. And we'll start with Council Member Whiting.

01:42:07.087 --> 01:42:10.196
Yes. Council Member Wood. Yes. Council Member Hewish. Yes.

01:42:10.612 --> 01:42:13.702
And Council Member Clark. Yes. And both Both motions pass.

01:42:14.156 --> 01:42:15.859
Thank you. All right,

01:42:19.199 --> 01:42:23.038
moving to items 14A, which is

01:42:23.215 --> 01:42:27.547
our first scheduled item. It's an ordinance of Eagle Mountain City rezoning

01:42:27.595 --> 01:42:31.016
certain loan— certain lands known as Corrigan Farms.

01:42:31.841 --> 01:42:35.369
Um, David has a presentation on this one.

01:42:38.002 --> 01:42:40.444
We, we did talk about this one in the work session a little bit,

01:42:40.460 --> 01:42:44.723
and we also saw this last meeting

01:42:44.981 --> 01:42:45.723
2 weeks ago?

01:42:54.331 --> 01:42:57.624
Was that from last weekend, David? I'm just— No, that was a

01:42:58.124 --> 01:43:01.609
year ago. Okay. We're still buckless this

01:43:02.109 --> 01:43:05.726
year. I was going to say congratulations. You know, I wasn't successful. We're still

01:43:05.774 --> 01:43:06.050
looking.

01:43:09.469 --> 01:43:12.918
Okay, Mayor and Council, this item you did have a

01:43:13.418 --> 01:43:18.155
public hearing on the previous meeting, October 6th, is for a rezone for

01:43:18.655 --> 01:43:22.241
the property known as Corrigan Farms. And just to brief you

01:43:22.741 --> 01:43:25.802
again, the property you see there in the red box, that is the property we're

01:43:26.302 --> 01:43:29.948
looking at tonight, used by QTS adjacent

01:43:30.448 --> 01:43:33.133
to the QTS subdivision, their property as well.

01:43:35.779 --> 01:43:39.514
Uh, look at the map first on the right. That is the property again there

01:43:39.562 --> 01:43:42.752
in the green square. The northeast and

01:43:43.252 --> 01:43:46.808
the south property is already zoned RTI,

01:43:47.657 --> 01:43:51.873
so the applicant is requesting the same overlay zone, the RTI overlay zone.

01:43:52.610 --> 01:43:55.960
Property to the west is Utah County, and again,

01:43:55.992 --> 01:43:57.964
there's approximately 41 acres.

01:43:58.637 --> 01:44:02.143
There's various uses that are approved, obviously. in the RTI zone,

01:44:02.968 --> 01:44:06.931
as well as some permitted accessory uses enumerated

01:44:07.431 --> 01:44:11.701
there on the screen. Again, you did have the public hearing on this previous

01:44:12.201 --> 01:44:15.888
meeting, and so the applicant requests the

01:44:16.388 --> 01:44:20.003
council consider this, and the Planning Commission does recommend approval of

01:44:20.503 --> 01:44:24.285
the rezone request. Is there

01:44:24.785 --> 01:44:28.666
any questions or comments from the council? Just to clarify, the property to the west

01:44:29.166 --> 01:44:31.878
is actually Fairfield Town, not— I was going to ask that. Yeah, it's what?

01:44:32.007 --> 01:44:35.685
Fairfield. Oh, it's Fair— oh, my apologies. We knew

01:44:35.942 --> 01:44:38.930
that. That's what I thought.

01:44:39.668 --> 01:44:43.218
So, but it's insignificant to this decision.

01:44:43.267 --> 01:44:47.379
So questions? The, uh, I mean, the staff report indicates,

01:44:47.587 --> 01:44:51.121
uh, the rezone would allow a potential develop— development

01:44:51.621 --> 01:44:54.694
of a data center with a natural gas power plant. And I think that latter,

01:44:55.000 --> 01:44:58.623
with the natural gas power plant stricken, I believe, given that the next

01:44:59.123 --> 01:45:02.137
agenda item— Yeah, that would be on the next slide, whatever Mark says. That would

01:45:02.169 --> 01:45:05.549
come through a separate application at a later date. That's their

01:45:06.049 --> 01:45:09.575
current intentions. Obviously, those could change over time. They wouldn't be getting any vesting

01:45:09.607 --> 01:45:11.942
in relation to any power plants on site.

01:45:15.985 --> 01:45:19.560
Councilmember Whiting, are you just asking that the That where

01:45:20.060 --> 01:45:23.213
it's written into the— on the

01:45:23.713 --> 01:45:27.077
agenda under the ordinance where it says with a natural gas

01:45:27.577 --> 01:45:31.091
plant, I mean, that that be stricken? Is that what you're saying? Well, I was

01:45:31.285 --> 01:45:34.362
just stating that it was— even though that was on the report, I think that

01:45:34.862 --> 01:45:37.388
was a carryover from the prior discussion.

01:45:38.789 --> 01:45:41.382
And I was just saying this more for the public benefit. Just don't— and you

01:45:41.882 --> 01:45:45.650
don't want to see that create some confusion? Correct. For the public's understanding of

01:45:46.150 --> 01:45:50.071
that. Yeah, this, this item's strictly the rezone. Yeah, just to clarify,

01:45:50.151 --> 01:45:53.279
the RTI zone doesn't have power plants as a

01:45:53.779 --> 01:45:57.416
permitted use. That was something that was being considered as part of the development agreement,

01:45:57.448 --> 01:45:59.854
and that is no longer in the development agreement. Got it. Okay,

01:46:00.110 --> 01:46:03.430
is there any other questions? If not,

01:46:03.446 --> 01:46:06.092
I'll call for a motion. And just to clear— yeah, just to clarify, yeah,

01:46:06.108 --> 01:46:09.973
we do not have any idea of anything, any future uses potentially.

01:46:10.037 --> 01:46:13.821
That could obviously go there with the RTI or It's just whatever's

01:46:14.321 --> 01:46:17.396
in the code as far as the overlay zone. Well, I think it's really important

01:46:17.896 --> 01:46:21.195
too for the residents that are listening. The RTI zone is very

01:46:21.323 --> 01:46:24.914
prescriptive. Like, you have to have X amount of square feet in your building,

01:46:25.331 --> 01:46:28.922
X amount of jobs have to be brought. Like, you can't have

01:46:29.274 --> 01:46:33.602
vapors or smells or all sorts of things. The city

01:46:34.102 --> 01:46:37.514
council that created that several years ago— I wasn't around

01:46:38.014 --> 01:46:42.284
then, but they put into it very specific things to protect

01:46:43.376 --> 01:46:47.313
our city from things that the people didn't want, period. So I think

01:46:47.813 --> 01:46:51.328
that's an important thing. It's not just a free pass. It's restrictive.

01:46:51.780 --> 01:46:55.459
I'll make the motion,

01:46:55.475 --> 01:46:58.950
Mayor. I move that the Eagle Mountain City Council approve

01:46:58.966 --> 01:47:02.400
the rezoning certain lands known as Corrigan Farms

01:47:02.432 --> 01:47:05.377
to— with the RTI overlay zone.

01:47:08.306 --> 01:47:10.414
We have a motion by Councilmember Wright.

01:47:12.427 --> 01:47:16.905
Second. Second by Councilmember Hewish. Any questions?

01:47:17.278 --> 01:47:21.236
Okay, we'll start the vote with Councilmember Wood. Yes. Councilmember Hewish.

01:47:21.381 --> 01:47:24.447
Yes. Councilmember Clark. Yes. Councilmember Wright. Yes.

01:47:24.560 --> 01:47:27.820
And Councilmember Whiting. Yes. Okay, that motion passes

01:47:27.917 --> 01:47:30.798
and we can go on to the next item. It's, uh, Ordinance Eagle Mountain City,

01:47:31.544 --> 01:47:34.869
approving the Corrigan Farms Development Agreement.

01:47:37.051 --> 01:47:40.818
Okay, so this would be the development agreement that goes along with the

01:47:40.947 --> 01:47:44.681
Corrigan Farms rezone. As stated earlier,

01:47:46.382 --> 01:47:50.311
this was brought before the council 2 weeks ago. There are certain feedback that was

01:47:50.811 --> 01:47:54.562
received from the council at that meeting, specifically regarding bringing any

01:47:54.755 --> 01:47:58.524
sort of power production through a separate application through the Alternative Energy

01:47:58.620 --> 01:48:01.809
Overlay Zone and associated development agreement associated with that.

01:48:02.466 --> 01:48:05.687
And that would be heard at some later date and decided on the merits of

01:48:06.187 --> 01:48:10.510
that alone. This is strictly for a data center use

01:48:11.119 --> 01:48:15.061
as being the primary use on the property in accordance with the RTI

